          "body": "In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs:9-23`, the water-column concentrations are captured once before the plant loop and then reused at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs:59-69`, even though each iteration mutates the shared water pools via `remove_plant_nutrients()` at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs:93-134`. Later guilds therefore compute nutrient limitation and health from stale TAN/nitrate/phosphate values after earlier guilds have already depleted the water column. Recompute the water-column factors inside the loop (or after each guild’s removals) so guild-to-guild competition uses current chemistry.",
